  "reviews": {},
  "roles": {},
  "rules": {},
  "sections": {
    "436583e4": {
      "body": "Same folder, same day, with the project index and /rpc/project:\n\n- /rpc/project: 6 KB (home() was 1.4 MB), 4 ms warm, 30 ms cold.\n- Opening the editor: no long task over 89 ms (was one of 561 ms); five tasks, 366 ms in all; heap 30 MB (was 48).\n- The editor no longer calls home(): the sidebar list, Cmd+P, link pickers, Uses, the project menu and use counts read one request per tab. Full documents load only when Play or a flow's board opens.\n- An unchanged design is never read or parsed again by the index (test: project.test.ts).\n\nStill to do: incremental imports and the watcher (phase 2), switching inside the tab (phase 3), thumbnails (phase 4).",
      "heading": "Measured, after phase 1",
      "id": "436583e4",
      "index": "a2"
    },
    "7abb39cd": {
      "body": "On this repo's designs folder (buni-redesign 1 MB, viewer 490 KB, core 91 KB), 2026-10-16:\n\n- home(): 1.4 MB of JSON (190 KB gzipped), 55 to 160 ms on the server; called by six parts of the editor, every LinkPicker mount included.\n- snapshot: 1.36 MB decoded, 22 to 90 ms.\n- Opening the editor: one 561 ms long task (284 ms in three tasks before the project features); heap 48 MB (was 30).\n- Every switch between designs is a full page load: bundle, snapshot and first render again.\n\nThe server is not the bottleneck; what it sends, how often, and the reload are.",
      "heading": "Measured, before",
      "id": "7abb39cd",
      "index": "a0"
    },
    "e4be356a": {
      "body": "1. Project index and /rpc/project: summaries, one store in the window, one subscription (phase 1).\n2. Versions on imports and memoised systems; the watcher pushes ProjectDelta (phase 2).\n3. Switching inside the tab from a snapshot cache keyed by path and version; selection and view kept per design; prefetch on hover (phase 3).\n4. Full documents only for Play and flows, prefetching the next design; cached thumbnails for Home (phase 4).\n\nAdvice from Codex (read-only review) agreed on the order: the index first, then incremental imports, then in-tab switching, then lazy documents.",
      "heading": "What changes, in order",
      "id": "e4be356a",
      "index": "a1"
    },
    "f37ae343": {
      "body": "Switching inside the tab (no page load; the stream moves to the new file; the last four designs drawn from a cache; the fresh copy shares every unchanged entry with it):\n\n- 1 MB designs (buni-redesign, viewer): 79 ms to a design not yet seen, 41 to 85 ms back to one seen; one long task of 54 ms across three switches (was a full page load, then a 561 ms task).\n- Harvest (small): 10 to 22 ms.\n- Back and forward move between the designs; an agent's edit to the design switched to shows live.\n\nTargets met: a warm switch under 150 ms; the editor never blocks 300 ms. Phase 2 (watcher, incremental imports) and phase 4 (thumbnails) remain.",
      "heading": "Measured, after phase 3",
      "id": "f37ae343",
      "index": "a3"
    }
  },
